      "content": "That feeling of detachment, like watching your life from afar, is incredibly painful and exhausting. When everything feels like dust, the desire for silence is a natural response to so much pain. If the noise is too much, perhaps we can focus on just one tiny moment of stillness, even if it's just breathing. Would you be willing to try focusing only on the sensation of air moving in and out of your body for just a moment?",
